-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/5b053419-b22a-5fe7-bd9c-6e7ebbeddd43
-- title:
--   Igusa rings trace to branch rings over (A₁,j₁), injectively
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $5 \le q$, $M'$ is a non-zero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and $A$ is a valuation subring of $\bar{\mathbb Q} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` lying over $q$ in the sense of `LiesOverPrime`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$; $\kappa =$ `ResidueField A` denotes its residue field. Two function fields inside Laurent series are in play: $\bar F =$ `fieldBar q M'`, the $\bar{\mathbb Q}$-subfield of `LaurentSeries (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)` generated by the coefficientwise image of the function field of level $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ with $H =$ `levelH q M'` the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$ (the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$); and `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, the corresponding base change to $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ of the full modular function field of level $M'$. The hypothesis `hle` asserts the inclusion `modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'`.
--
--   Further data of the frame: a finite set $W$ of places (in the sense of the project's `Place`: a valuation subring of the function field containing the constants, distinct from the whole field, whose ring is a principal ideal ring) of `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` over $\kappa$ — the field generated over $\kappa$ by the $q$-expansions `jqModC` and `jqNModC` of $j$ and of $j$ at level $M'$ — with `hW` saying that $W$ is exactly the set `ssPlaces q M' κ` of supersingular places, namely the rational places $w$ satisfying the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace` for which $w$'s evaluation of `jGeomGen` lies in `ssJSet q κ`, the set of $j$ such that every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\kappa$ with that $j$-invariant has only the zero point killed by $q$. Next, $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'`: a valuation subring `R₀.integers`, a surjective residue homomorphism onto `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` whose kernel is the maximal ideal, restricting to $A$ on the constants and inducing the residue map of $A$ there, the existence for each non-zero $f$ of a constant scaling landing in `R₀.integers` with non-zero residue, together with a map `R₀.placeMap` on places preserving degrees and transporting divisors of functions to divisors of their residues. The hypothesis `hR₀` requires compatibility with coefficientwise reduction: for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose image in `LaurentSeries (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)` lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that image lies in `R₀.integers` and its $R_0$-residue is, as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. Finally $\zeta$ is an element of `Idx q`, that is a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\bar{\mathbb Q}$, and two families of valuation subrings of $\bar F$ are given: $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{Ig}} =$ `OIg` indexed by [`CuspidalType.ProjLine q`](def/CuspidalType_IsCuspidalOfType.html#L21) $= \mathbb P^1(\mathbb F_q)$, and $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{SS}} =$ `OSS` indexed by $W$.
--
--   The Igusa hypotheses are four. `hIg_inf` describes $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ at the line `lineInfty q` $= [1:0]$ as a Gauss ring: $f \in \mathcal O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ if and only if there are Laurent series $x, y$ with coefficients in $A$ such that the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ is non-zero and $f \cdot y = x$ in `LaurentSeries (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)`. `hIg` says each line $\lambda$ is obtained from $\infty$ by some $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, in the sense that the image `redQ q γ` of $\gamma$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb F_q)$ carries $[1:0]$ to $\lambda$, and that $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\lambda)$ is the pullback of $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ along the automorphism `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` of $\bar F$ over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$. `hIg_inj` asserts that $\lambda \mapsto \mathcal O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\lambda)$ is injective, and `hIg_perm` that for every $\zeta'$ in `Idx q` and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ there is a permutation $\sigma$ of $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb F_q)$ with $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\lambda)$ pulled back along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` equal to $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\sigma\lambda)$ for all $\lambda$.
--
--   The supersingular hypotheses are four. `hSS_A` says that, for each $s \in W$, a constant $x \in \bar{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ exactly when $x \in A$. `hSS_over` says that, for $s \in W$ and $f \in$ `R₀.integers` such that $f$ has non-negative order at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ at which the class of `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) jq` (the $j$-function) has non-negative order, if the $R_0$-residue of $f$ lies in the valuation ring of the place $s$, then the image of $f$ in $\bar F$ lies in $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ and, for every $a \in A$ whose residue equals the value of $s$ at the $R_0$-residue of $f$, the difference of the image of $f$ and of $a$ lies in $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ and in its maximal ideal. `hSS_fix` says each $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ is invariant under pullback along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` for all $\zeta'$ and all $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, and `hSS_tr` provides for each $s$ a transversal element $t \in \mathcal O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ such that $t - a$ lies in $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ and is a unit there for every $a \in A$. In addition, $R$ is a `RegularProlongation` of $A$ from $\bar F$ to `xHFunctionFieldC κ (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')` (the same package as a constant reduction, without the place map: a valuation subring with surjective residue map onto that field, kernel the maximal ideal, agreeing with $A$ on constants, plus the scaling property), with `hR` asserting `R.integers = OIg (lineInfty q)`, and `hR₀O` asserting that $f \in$ `R₀.integers` if and only if the image of $f$ in $\bar F$ lies in $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$.
--
--   The hypotheses on the constants are: an element $\pi \in A$ with $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$; a subfield $k_0$ of $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ lying in $A$, such that $A \cap k_0$ (the comap of $A$ along $k_0 \to \bar{\mathbb Q}$) is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, is henselian and has algebraically closed residue field, and such that every $a \in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0 \cap A$ (`hκ`); an auxiliary prime $\ell$ with $3 \le \ell$, $\ell \ne q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$, an element $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ which is a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity, and an element $\varpi_t \in k_0$ lying in $A$ with $\varpi_t^{q^2-1} = q u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$; and finally a subfield $K_1$ of $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ containing $k_0$ and finite over it, together with a valuation subring $A_1$ of $K_1$ consisting exactly of the elements of $K_1$ lying in $A$, which is a henselian discrete valuation ring.
--
--   The conclusion is stated for the $k_0$-algebra structure on $\bar F$ obtained by composing $k_0 \hookrightarrow \bar{\mathbb Q}$ with $\bar{\mathbb Q} \to \bar F$, and is quantified over a $k_0$-subfield $F_0$ of $\bar F$ subject to four conditions: (i) the $k_0$-subfield generated by the constants $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ together with $F_0$ is all of $\bar F$; (ii) $F_0$ is stable under every `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; (iii) a linear disjointness condition: for every $k_0$-subfield $K'$ of $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ finite over $k_0$, every $m$, every family $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \bar{\mathbb Q}$ linearly independent over $K'$ and every family $a : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \bar F$ with all $a_i$ in the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K'$ together with $F_0$, the relation $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ forces $a_i = 0$ for all $i$; (iv) every element of $\bar F$ whose underlying Laurent series has rational coefficients, i.e. lies in the range of `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)`, belongs to $F_0$.
--
--   Write $T_1$ for the $k_0$-subfield `IntermediateField.adjoin k₀ (algebraMap (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) (fieldBar q M') '' K₁) ⊔ F₀` of $\bar F$. The conclusion is further quantified over an $A_1$-algebra structure on $T_1$ whose structure map is compatible with the inclusions, in the sense that the image in $\bar F$ of $a \in A_1$ under `algebraMap A₁ T₁` equals the image of $a$ under $\bar{\mathbb Q} \to \bar F$, and over a non-zero element $j_1$ of $T_1$ whose image in $\bar F$ is the inclusion of the class of `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) jq`, that is, the $j$-function.
--
--   Before the conclusion the statement introduces six local abbreviations attached to the two-chart integral model [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A₁ T₁ j₁`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout gluing $\mathrm{Spec}$ of `chartAlgFin` (the elements of $T_1$ integral over $A_1[j_1]$) and $\mathrm{Spec}$ of `chartAlgInf` (the elements integral over $A_1[j_1^{-1}]$) along the middle chart. For a point $x$ of the model and $f \in T_1$: `InStalk x f` says that over every point $y$ of `XFin` mapping to $x$ under `ιFin` there are $g, h$ in `chartAlgFin` with $h \notin y$ and $f h = g$, and likewise on the infinite chart; `InMax x f` is the same with the additional requirement $g \in y$. For a place $P$ of $\bar F$ over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$, `Centred P x` says that $P$ is rational (the constants surject onto its residue field) and that every $f$ with `InStalk x f` lies in the valuation ring of $P$, has $P$-value in $A$, and that this value has $A$-valuation $< 1$ precisely when `InMax x f` holds. `GoodPt x` says that $x$ maps to the closed point of $\mathrm{Spec}\,A_1$ under `toBase`, that $x$ is closed (any $y$ to which $x$ specialises equals $x$), that on both charts every chart element whose image in $\bar F$ is a non-unit of `R.integers` lies in the prime corresponding to any point above $x$, and that for every point $y$ of `XFin` above $x$, every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from `chartAlgFin` with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j_1)$ is not a supersingular $j$-invariant, i.e. does not lie in `ssJSet q Ω`. For a place $Q$ of `xHFunctionFieldC κ (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')` over $\kappa$, `Reads x Q` says that every $f$ with `InStalk x f` lies in `R.integers`, that its $R$-residue lies in the valuation ring of $Q$, and that this residue is a non-unit there precisely when `InMax x f`. Finally `OffBranch x` says that for every line $\lambda \ne [1:0]$ and every point $y$ above $x$ on either chart there is a chart element whose image in $\bar F$ is a non-unit of $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\lambda)$ and which does not lie in $y$. The four conjuncts of the conclusion do not refer to these six abbreviations.
--
--   The conclusion asserts the conjunction of the following four statements, in which $\lambda, \lambda'$ range over [`CuspidalType.ProjLine q`](def/CuspidalType_IsCuspidalOfType.html#L21) (written $\ell$ in the Lean, shadowing the auxiliary prime).
--
--   First: for every line $\lambda$ and every $a \in A_1$, the image of $a$ in $T_1$, viewed in $\bar F$, lies in $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\lambda)$.
--
--   Second: for every line $\lambda$ and every $a$ in the maximal ideal of $A_1$, that image is a non-unit of $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\lambda)$.
--
--   Third: for every line $\lambda$ and every polynomial $P \in A_1[X]$ whose coefficientwise reduction modulo the maximal ideal of $A_1$ is non-zero, the element $P(j_1)$ of $T_1$, viewed in $\bar F$, lies in $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\lambda)$, and so does the inverse $P(j_1)^{-1}$ formed in $T_1$.
--
--   Fourth: for all lines $\lambda, \lambda'$, if for every $f \in T_1$ the image of $f$ in $\bar F$ lies in $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\lambda)$ if and only if it lies in $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\lambda')$, then $\lambda = \lambda'$.
--
--   The four clauses express that the trace of each Igusa valuation ring $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\lambda)$ on the level field $T_1 = K_1 \cdot F_0$ satisfies the axioms of a branch ring over the pair $(A_1, j_1)$ — it contains $A_1$, sends the maximal ideal of $A_1$ into its non-units, and makes $P(j_1)$ a unit for every $P \in A_1[X]$ with non-zero reduction — and that the $q+1$ Igusa lines are still separated after restriction to $T_1$. In the Igusa-model part of the construction these facts feed the statements that produce maximal ideals of the chart algebras, rational places of the descent and localisations of the chart algebras realising the Igusa rings.
